§§ `נספח ה' קביעת דרגה והמרות שכר`

-- ¶2-¶4: an existing teacher's grade is set by converting the salary, by
-- personal data, roles and the stage taught before joining; a new teacher
-- is placed directly at grade 1 by education and role, with no conversion
-- (and 1(ד) note 1: a new academic, after the internship, at grade 1 and
-- seniority 1).
@ref akn:att_5__hc_1/p1 akn:att_5__hc_1/p2 akn:att_5__hc_1/p3 akn:att_5__hc_1/p4 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_d__cls_1
GIVEN t IS A `special-education teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the salary is converted for` t IF
    `an existing teacher` t

`the grade a new teacher is placed at` MEANS 1
`the seniority a new academic is placed at after the internship` MEANS 1

-- 1(א), 2(א), 3(א): A = X × (100 + Y) / 100. (The deputies' formula is not
-- in the text, only its legend; their worked example applies the same.)
@ref akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_a akn:att_5__hc_1__para_2 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_2__subpara_a akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_a
GIVEN `salary to convert` IS A NUMBER @desc X, in shekels
      `conversion coefficient` IS A NUMBER @desc Y, in percent
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `converted salary` `salary to convert` `conversion coefficient` IS
    `salary to convert` TIMES (100 PLUS `conversion coefficient`) DIVIDED BY 100

-- 1(ב): X for a teacher is a 100% position's March salary (the year
-- before joining; the joining month where March had no employment) in the
-- combined salary, the 87, 94, 2001, 2008 and 2011 supplements, and the
-- role allowances that do not continue: split, training, in-service,
-- double degree, cost of living. 1(ד) note 2: one on unpaid leave or
-- sabbatical that year takes September of the transition year.
@ref akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p1 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p2 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p3 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p4 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p5 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p6 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_d__cls_2
GIVEN `March salary components` IS A NUMBER @desc the listed components as paid that March, in shekels
      `position fraction that March` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `salary to convert at 100%` `March salary components` `position fraction that March` IS
    `March salary components` DIVIDED BY `position fraction that March`

-- The coefficient table for academic teachers (¶7) is not in the corpus
-- (corpus defect): Y is an input. ¶12: a non-academic's coefficient is
-- the academic one × 0.8. ¶13-¶14: for primary-school teachers of grades
-- 7-9 on a 24-hour base, "מקדם ההמרה יגדל ב-12.5%" — F-2020-21_tashpa_01-f.
@ref akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p7 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p12
GIVEN `academic coefficient` IS A NUMBER @desc the coefficient of the (missing) table for academic teachers, in percent
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `non-academic coefficient` `academic coefficient` IS
    `academic coefficient` TIMES 0.8

-- The reading adopted (F-2020-21_tashpa_01-f): a relative rise, the
-- coefficient times 1.125; such teachers work the primary week (¶14).
@ref akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p13 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p14
GIVEN `coefficient` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `coefficient for grades 7-9 in a primary school` `coefficient` IS
    `"grows by 12.5%" read as a share` `coefficient`

`the week of a grades 7-9 teacher in a primary school` MEANS `the primary special-education week`

GIVEN `coefficient` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `"grows by 12.5%" read as a share` `coefficient` IS
    `coefficient` TIMES 1.125

GIVEN `coefficient` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `"grows by 12.5%" read as points` `coefficient` IS
    `coefficient` PLUS 12.5

`the two readings of "יגדל ב-12.5%" differ` MEANS
    NOT (`"grows by 12.5%" read as a share` 17 EQUALS `"grows by 12.5%" read as points` 17)
#ASSERT `the two readings of "יגדל ב-12.5%" differ`

-- akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p8 The next page's letterhead; no rule.
-- akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p9 Letterhead; no rule.
-- akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p10 Letterhead; no rule.
-- akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p11 Letterhead; no rule.

-- 1(ד): an academic is placed in the academic table by total seniority at
-- the grade whose salary is nearest A, equal or above (the tables are
-- linked, not printed: the placed salary is an input). 2(ה), 3(ה): the
-- same in the first deputies' and principals' tables by complexity level.
@ref akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_d akn:att_5__hc_1__para_2__subpara_e akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p1 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p2 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p3
GIVEN `grade salaries` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc the salaries of the grades of the right table, at the employee's seniority or complexity level
      `converted` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `grade salaries at or above` `grade salaries` `converted` IS
    filter (GIVEN g YIELD g AT LEAST `converted`) `grade salaries`

-- F-2020-21_tashpa_01-h: the rule places at the grade nearest A, "equal or
-- above"; it does not say where A is above every grade of the table. The
-- reading adopted: the table's highest grade, as example 2 places the
-- deputy (grade ד', below A).
GIVEN `grade salaries` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `converted` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `placed salary` `grade salaries` `converted` IS
    IF null (`grade salaries at or above` `grade salaries` `converted`)
    THEN maximum `grade salaries`
    ELSE minimum (`grade salaries at or above` `grade salaries` `converted`)

-- 2(ב)-(ג): a first deputy's Y is 20%; X is the March salary at 100% but
-- for the education allowance, expense refunds, sundry payments and tax
-- gross-ups. 3(ב)-(ג): a principal's Y is 15%; X likewise, but for expense
-- refunds, yearly payments and tax gross-ups. Either, absent that March on
-- unpaid leave or sabbatical, takes September of the transition year.
@ref akn:att_5__hc_1__para_2__subpara_b akn:att_5__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p1 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p2 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p3
`first deputy's coefficient` MEANS 20

GIVEN `March salary but the excluded items` IS A NUMBER @desc the first deputy's salary that March (September of the transition year, for one on unpaid leave or sabbatical), but for the education allowance, expense refunds, sundry payments, tax gross-ups and taxable benefits, in shekels
      `position fraction that March` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a first deputy's salary to convert` `March salary but the excluded items` `position fraction that March` IS
    `salary to convert at 100%` `March salary but the excluded items` `position fraction that March`

@ref akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_b akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_c/p1 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_c/p2 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_c/p3
`principal's coefficient` MEANS 15

GIVEN `March salary but the excluded items` IS A NUMBER @desc the principal's salary that March (September of the transition year, for one on unpaid leave or sabbatical), but for expense refunds, yearly payments, tax gross-ups and taxable benefits, in shekels
      `position fraction that March` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a principal's salary to convert` `March salary but the excluded items` `position fraction that March` IS
    `salary to convert at 100%` `March salary but the excluded items` `position fraction that March`

-- 3(ה) ¶4-¶15: a principal employed above 100% and up to 150% gets a
-- personal supplement: B = T × (100 + Y) / 100, T being the March salary
-- at the whole position (March before the leave, for one on leave); C = B
-- − the new tabular salary, turned into a percentage of the principal's
-- combined salary.
@ref akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p4 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p5 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p6 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p7 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p8 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p9 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p10 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p11 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p12 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p13 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p14 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p15
GIVEN `position fraction` IS A NUMBER @desc the principal's whole position (1 = 100%)
      `T` IS A NUMBER @desc the March salary at the whole position, in shekels
      `new tabular salary` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the principal's personal supplement as a share` `position fraction` `T` `new tabular salary` IS
    IF `position fraction` GREATER THAN 1 AND `position fraction` AT MOST 1.5
    THEN `personal supplement as a share` `T` `new tabular salary`
    ELSE 0

GIVEN `T` IS A NUMBER @desc the March salary at the whole position, in shekels
      `new tabular salary` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `personal supplement in shekels` `T` `new tabular salary` IS
    `converted salary` `T` `principal's coefficient` MINUS `new tabular salary`

GIVEN `T` IS A NUMBER, `new tabular salary` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `personal supplement as a share` `T` `new tabular salary` IS
    `personal supplement in shekels` `T` `new tabular salary` DIVIDED BY `new tabular salary`

-- The worked examples, as printed.

-- Example 1 (1(ב)-(ד)): an academic mother teaching junior high at 0.9.
@ref akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p15 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p16 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p17 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p18 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p19 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p20 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p21 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p22 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p23 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p24 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p25 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p26 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p27 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p28
`example 1's components` MEANS
    LIST 3779.38, 141.21, 113.38, 187.25, 259.08, 157.03, 268.82, 900.54, 298.69

#ASSERT sum `example 1's components` EQUALS 6105.38

@ref akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p29 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p30 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p31 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_c
-- X as printed (6,105.38 / 0.9, cut to the agora); the steps below use it.
`example 1's X` MEANS 6783.75
`example 1's Y` MEANS 34
`example 1's printed A` MEANS 9399.29

-- F-2020-21_tashpa_01-e: every example multiplies X by 1.034 ("תוספת
-- שחיקה") before the formula; neither the formula nor X's definition has
-- that factor, and the formula alone does not give the printed A.
`erosion factor of the examples` MEANS 1.034

GIVEN `printed` IS A NUMBER, `computed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `within an agora of` `printed` `computed` IF
    `computed` MINUS `printed` AT MOST 0.01 AND `printed` MINUS `computed` AT MOST 0.01

`the formula alone does not give example 1's A` MEANS
        (NOT `within an agora of` `example 1's printed A` (`converted salary` `example 1's X` `example 1's Y`))
    AND `within an agora of` `example 1's printed A` (`converted salary` (`example 1's X` TIMES `erosion factor of the examples`) `example 1's Y`)
#ASSERT `the formula alone does not give example 1's A`

-- The reading adopted (F-2020-21_tashpa_01-e): the examples' factor is
-- applied, as the Ministry computes A; it is a named input of the
-- conversion, the circular giving no rule for it.
GIVEN `salary to convert` IS A NUMBER, `coefficient` IS A NUMBER, `erosion factor` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `converted salary as the examples compute it` `salary to convert` `coefficient` `erosion factor` IS
    `converted salary` (`salary to convert` TIMES `erosion factor`) `coefficient`

-- The example's placement: seniority 10 (8 years' teaching and 21 months'
-- army), grade 6 at 9,670.70 — at or above A.
#ASSERT 9670.70 AT LEAST `example 1's printed A`
#ASSERT `within an agora of` `example 1's X` (`salary to convert at 100%` 6105.38 0.9)

