§§ `Worked examples`

-- Seniority, ages and positions are placeholders.
`an existing academic at a third` MEANS
    `special-education teacher` WITH
        `recognised years of actual teaching` IS 6
        `seniority in teaching`              IS 6
        `holds an academic degree`           IS TRUE
        `holds a teaching certificate`       IS TRUE
        `position fraction`                  IS 0.34
        `in special education`               IS TRUE
        `signed the academic-studies commitment` IS FALSE
        `approved as an exception`           IS FALSE
        `an intern`                          IS FALSE
        `a health-profession or arts therapist` IS FALSE
        `teacher age`                        IS 35

`a non-academic of 20 years who has not signed` MEANS
    `special-education teacher` WITH
        `recognised years of actual teaching` IS 20
        `seniority in teaching`              IS 20
        `holds an academic degree`           IS FALSE
        `holds a teaching certificate`       IS TRUE
        `position fraction`                  IS 1
        `in special education`               IS TRUE
        `signed the academic-studies commitment` IS FALSE
        `approved as an exception`           IS FALSE
        `an intern`                          IS FALSE
        `a health-profession or arts therapist` IS FALSE
        `teacher age`                        IS 48

#ASSERT `joins the reform` `an existing academic at a third`
#ASSERT NOT `joins the reform` `a non-academic of 20 years who has not signed`
#ASSERT `the age reduction` `an existing teacher aged 55` EQUALS `age reduction` 3 1 32
#ASSERT `the work week for` `multi-stage school` 8 EQUALS `the post-primary special-education week`
#ASSERT `who approves` 1.1 EQUALS `exceptional placement in the placement system`
#ASSERT `frontal hours at level` `the principal's frontal hours` 5 EQUALS 8
#ASSERT `placed salary` (LIST 9000, 9670.70, 10100) 9399.29 EQUALS 9670.70
#ASSERT `placed salary` (LIST 16500, 17200, 17961.60) 18136.311 EQUALS 17961.60
#ASSERT `the counsellor's least frontal teaching` 1 EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `the counsellor's least frontal teaching` 0.5 EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `the mother's reduction` `a mother back from leave at 90%` EQUALS `five nursing hours a week off the stay hours`
#ASSERT `role allowances paid` (LIST 0.10, 0.06, 0.03) EQUALS 0.16
#ASSERT `the אופק חדש advance` `a principal` 10000 1 EQUALS 1500
#ASSERT `work counts from minute` 450 EQUALS 465
#ASSERT `the principal's personal supplement as a share` 1.5 `example 3's T` 20359.87 EQUALS `personal supplement as a share` `example 3's T` 20359.87
#ASSERT `the principal's personal supplement as a share` 1 `example 3's T` 20359.87 EQUALS 0

-- Every week of section 4 adds up to its 36 hours.
GIVEN h IS A `week hours`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `adds up` h IF
    h's `frontal hours` PLUS h's `individual hours` PLUS h's `stay hours` EQUALS h's `total hours`

#ASSERT all `adds up` (LIST `the teacher's week` `the primary special-education week`,
                            `the teacher's week` `the post-primary special-education week`,
                            `the therapist's week` `the primary special-education week`,
                            `the therapist's week` `the post-primary special-education week`)

-- Each complexity table of section 9 has one row per level from 3 to 8,
-- and stays within the range its clause prints (9.2: 6-9; 9.7.1: 18-21;
-- 9.7.2: 9-11; 9.7.3: 13-15).
GIVEN `table` IS A LIST OF `complexity row`
      `low` IS A NUMBER
      `high` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `within its printed range` `table` `low` `high` IF
        count `table` EQUALS 6
    AND all (GIVEN r YIELD r's `frontal teaching hours` AT LEAST `low` AND r's `frontal teaching hours` AT MOST `high`) `table`

#ASSERT `within its printed range` `the principal's frontal hours` 6 9
#ASSERT `within its printed range` `the primary first deputy's frontal hours` 18 21
#ASSERT `within its printed range` `the post-primary first deputy's frontal hours` 9 11
#ASSERT `within its printed range` `the multi-stage first deputy's frontal hours` 13 15

#TRACE `completing the academic degree` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the teaching employee` DOES `present proof of an academic degree` AT 40
#TRACE `completing the academic degree` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the teaching employee` DOES `present proof of an academic degree` AT 60
#TRACE `completing the internship requirements` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the teaching employee` DOES `complete the degree and the teaching certificate` AT 18
#TRACE `paying the advance` 1500 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `pay the אופק חדש advance` 1500 AT 1
#TRACE `no more than 18 activity hours a half` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the school principal` DOES `allocate school-activity hours` 20 AT 2
